    Lines:
      Loved:
      - 'Haddock. Now there is a fish a man can have for his supper without a speech about it. Thank you.'
      Liked:
      - 'Flounder. My wife does them in the pan with butter. You have made a friend at home as well.'
      Neutral:
      - 'Well. That is kind of you. I will find it a corner of the cooler.'
      Disliked:
      - 'A green crab. They eat everything worth having in the bay. Are you giving it to me or getting rid of it?'
